    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1071">

                <pb facs="1430" n="1420" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/12–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Myers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Teintsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-16T16:00:00+08:00">December 16,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 17—12:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>30. [To Embassy:] War Transportation Board removed from Frazar premises 97 cases
                    motor car parts, 96 tires, 20 batteries and 153 tins on [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of</hi>] carbide on December 14 (Embassy’s 2137 of December 11, 10 a.m. and
                    my telegram No. 28, December 14, 4 p.m.), notwithstanding Consulate General’s
                    prior request to cease removals and return goods already removed.</p>
                <p>Stevens,<anchor n="62" xml:id="d1071-f1"/> Peiping, informed in memorandum dated
                    December 12 from Generalissimo’s Headquarters, Peiping, that Yorkson Shen had
                    requested General Li Tsung-jen to order General Chiang Shih-yi to stop
                    “disturbing the goods of the Karagheusian Wool Company”, which order has been
                    issued.</p>
                <p>Sent to Embassy, repeated to Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Myers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1071-f1" n="62" xml:id="d1071-f1-content">
                <p>Harry E. Stevens, Second Secretary of Embassy in China and Consul on detail to
                    Peiping.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
